:knockdown  rdfs:comment  "Gene knockdown refers to techniques by which the expression of one or more of an organism's genes is reduced, either through genetic modification (a change in the DNA of one of the organism's chromosomes) or by treatment with a reagent such as a short DNA or RNA oligonucleotide with a sequence complementary to either an mRNA transcript or a gene." ;
        rdfs:subClassOf  :Gene_Perturbation ;
        rdf:type         owl:Class .

